# Background and Delayed Job Processing Rules

## When to Check These Rules
- When implementing background tasks
- When processing long-running operations
- When handling asynchronous operations
- When scheduling delayed jobs
- When working with Sidekiq workers

## Job Processing
- Use Sidekiq exclusively (location: app/sidekiq)
- Never use ActiveJob or app/jobs
- Follow Sidekiq best practices
- Implement proper error handling
- Use appropriate retry strategies
- Consider job priority and queue selection
- Monitor job performance and queue sizes
- Implement proper job timeouts
- Handle job dependencies appropriately

## Error Handling
- Implement proper error handling in jobs
- Use appropriate retry strategies
- Log job failures with context
- Handle job timeouts gracefully
- Implement dead letter queues for failed jobs
- Monitor job failure rates
- Alert on critical job failures

## Examples

✅ Correct:
```ruby
# Proper Sidekiq worker
class UserEmailWorker
  include Sidekiq::Worker
  sidekiq_options queue: :high_priority, retry: 3

  def perform(user_id)
    user = User.find(user_id)
    UserMailer.welcome_email(user).deliver_now
  rescue ActiveRecord::RecordNotFound => e
    logger.error "Failed to send welcome email: #{e.message}"
    raise
  end
end

# Proper job scheduling
UserEmailWorker.perform_async(user.id)
UserEmailWorker.perform_in(1.hour, user.id)
```

❌ Incorrect:
- Using ActiveJob instead of Sidekiq
- Not handling errors properly
- No retry strategy
- Poor job organization
- No proper logging
- Missing job timeouts
- No queue management

## Common Mistakes to Avoid
- Using ActiveJob instead of Sidekiq
- Not implementing proper error handling
- No retry strategy
- Poor job organization
- No proper logging
- Missing job timeouts
- No queue management
- Not monitoring job performance
- Not handling job dependencies
- Not implementing dead letter queues

## Validation Checklist
- [ ] Sidekiq is used exclusively
- [ ] Proper error handling is implemented
- [ ] Appropriate retry strategies are in place
- [ ] Jobs are properly organized
- [ ] Proper logging is implemented
- [ ] Job timeouts are set
- [ ] Queue management is in place
- [ ] Job performance is monitored
- [ ] Job dependencies are handled
- [ ] Dead letter queues are implemented
